-- title:
--   Ordinary corner of p-torsion spans inside τ(e) Ω
-- statement:
--   Fix an odd prime $p$ and $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$; let $S$ be a set of naturals and assume the Hecke–diamond inputs [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsHAll M H`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L113) (the Hecke input package at every prime $\ell$ together with, for each $d$, a diamond automorphism of the function field of $X_H(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$). Write $J = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of that function field and $T_pJ$ for its Tate module (sequences $(x_n)$ with $p^n x_n = 0$, $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$). Let $\mathbb{T}$ be a commutative $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra acting on $T_pJ$ compatibly with $\mathbb{Z}_p$ and faithfully, let $\mathrm{op} : \mathrm{Gen}\,M\,S \to \mathbb{T}$ send each generator $g$ to an element acting as the operator induced on $T_pJ$ by [`ModularCurve.genOpH M H S g`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L80), and assume the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-subalgebra generated by the image of $\mathrm{op}$ is all of $\mathbb{T}$. Let $S'$ be an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb{T}$ (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$, maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting the maximal spectrum, with $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j$ exactly for $i \ne j$) and $i_0$ an index with $\mathrm{op}(U_p) \notin \mathfrak{m}_{i_0}$. Let $Pl$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ in its nonunits, and $P_0$ a $\mathbb{T}$-submodule of $T_pJ$ whose elements are exactly those in the corner $e_{i_0} \cdot T_pJ$ on which the inertia subgroup at $Pl$ acts through the $p$-adic cyclotomic character. Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, let $\Omega_1 =$ [`ModularCurve.ssPolarDifferentials K (CohCarrier.GammaH (M/p) (ModularCurve.infSubgroup p M H hpM)) p`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L35) (differentials regular away from the supersingular places and with at most simple poles there), and let $\tau : \mathbb{T} \to \mathrm{End}_K \Omega_1$ be a ring homomorphism with $\tau(\mathrm{op}\,g)\,\omega = \mathrm{genDiffModL}\,g\,\omega$ for all generators $g$ and all $\omega$. Finally let $\Theta$ be an additive map from the $p$-torsion of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ to $\Omega_1$ satisfying $\Theta(y) = \mathrm{genDiffModL}\,g\,(\Theta x)$ whenever $y$ is the image of $x$ under [`ModularCurve.genOpH M H S g`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L80). Then the $K$-span of the image under $\Theta$ of those $p$-torsion classes lying in the image of the corner $e_{i_0} \cdot T_pJ$ under the level-one projection $T_pJ \to J$ is contained in the range of $\tau(e_{i_0})$.
--
--   This is the transfer step in the ordinary part of the Ihara/level-lowering argument: it says that a Hecke-equivariant additive map from $J_H(M)[p]$ to the supersingular polar differentials of $X_{H'}(M/p)$ in characteristic $p$ carries the ordinary idempotent corner into the corresponding corner $\tau(e_{i_0})\Omega_1$ of differentials, the compatibility being forced by the fact that $\mathbb{T}$ is generated over $\mathbb{Z}_p$ by the operators $\mathrm{op}\,g$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_addMonoidHom_torsion_ssPolarDifferentials_dlog_of_ordinary_of_mem_infSubgroup`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_addMonoidHom_torsion_ssPolarDifferentials_dlog_of_ordinary_of_mem_infSubgroup), where the map $\Theta$ is produced from the $\mathrm{dlog}$ construction.
